WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.420
Hello and welcome to Conan
O'Brien Needs a Friend,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.140
a never-ending quest to find someone

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.623
who will meet with me
outside of a podcast studio.

00:00:10.623 --> 00:00:12.300
You'll get there.
And share a bowl of soup.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.650
Everyone in here, have you noticed this?

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.078
Everybody in here talks a good game.

00:00:16.078 --> 00:00:16.911
Yeah.

00:00:16.911 --> 00:00:18.780
But not much happens
outside the podcast studio,

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.910
and the times that I reach out...

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.700
Well, let's just say,
I don't hear much back.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.990
Really, there have been a couple times

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.090
where you've actually
had a thing with a guest,

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.860
like, "I'm really gonna talk to you,

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.420
we're gonna go out to dinner"
and that kind of thing,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.490
and those have not happened.
Yeah, exactly.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.550
And that's something I learned
in the old late night game.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.080
Years and years ago.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.360
I'd get fooled because they'd come out,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.840
we'd welcome the guest, and
the guest would come out,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.240
the star would come out and
they'd lock eyes with me

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.240
and smile and embrace me and
sit and hang on every word.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.590
And those are all the cues that you get

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.852
in high school when
someone really likes you.

00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:55.685
Mm.

00:00:55.685 --> 00:00:58.020
But I'm in a fake environment.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:58.853
Yeah.

00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:00.007
And so, afterwards, I'd think,

00:01:00.007 --> 00:01:03.089
"You know who really
likes me? Harrison Ford."

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:04.290
(people laughing)

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.123
That's gotta be tough.

00:01:05.123 --> 00:01:08.220
He thinks I'm the bee's
knees. He hung on every word.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.033
And then, later on, when I
see him squeezing avocados,

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.920
and I jump out and say,
"It's me, your old buddy!"

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.070
And hug him, suddenly I'm
getting karate chopped

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.240
in the throat?
Right.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.434
By a rugged leading man. That's not right.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:25.267
No.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.700
Now some people have said, "Don't jump out

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.200
at people and hug them."
Right, right.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.720
Approach quietly and introduce
yourself as a grownup.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.500
But no, I think the flaw is not with me.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.150
Well, you said in the very beginning

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.010
you wanna share a bowl of soup.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.380
So I think that's problematic too.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.127
I don't think you should
text people and be like,

00:01:42.127 --> 00:01:44.100
"Hey, you wanna share a bowl of soup?"

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.040
Something that involves
slurping and hunched shoulders.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.353
And germs going into the same bowl.

00:01:50.331 --> 00:01:53.310
I don't know, you gotta
get a new approach.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.870
Yeah, why don't you do what
everybody else is doing

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.640
and play pickleball or something?

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.993
Yeah, you know what, I don't
know this pickleball thing.

00:01:58.993 --> 00:01:59.826
Oh.

00:01:59.826 --> 00:02:01.200
And I've had people explain it to me.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.730
My sister-in-law is deep.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.900
And I know that it's
become kind of a mania.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.733
Yeah.

00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:07.140
Everyone's playing pickleball.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.980
My only question is do you
have to take off your shirt?

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.430
What?
Why?

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.250
I saw a photograph somewhere
of people playing pickleball

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.110
and they were all stripped to the waist.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.780
Just the fellas, but I thought,
"Well, I can't take off--"

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.310
I think that was hide the pickle.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.143
What's that?

00:02:21.143 --> 00:02:22.470
I think that was hide the pickle.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:26.460
You always go to the same
place. You dirty, dirty man.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.100
I always have to be
dressed, like in a suit.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.508
Right.
Whenever I play.

00:02:30.508 --> 00:02:33.240
Like a full business suit.
Like a real jock.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.140
Like a business suit.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.160
Oh.
[Conan] Yeah.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.470
No, I don't know anything about the game,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.000
but people go nuts for it.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.440
Yeah, it's sweeping the nation.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.278
Well, it sounds like a room
full of non-pickleball players.

00:02:43.278 --> 00:02:45.180
I've played it a couple times, I'm sorry,

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.920
I mean I have played it with--

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.450
my sister-in-law is really into it,

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.820
and when you get into it, you get into it.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.550
I think it's like playing tennis,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.410
but it's not as much movement,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.653
and so, it's still athletic,
but it's not like tennis.

00:02:56.653 --> 00:03:00.590
and so, it's still athletic,
but it's not like tennis.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.280
Is it just boomer tennis?

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.567
It might be kind of boomer tennis--

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.550
It's slacker tennis.
Yeah.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.140
I think it's tennis, but no one has

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.890
to really move and at any
moment you could just walk away

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.360
but still insist on getting paid.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.560
And it's doubles, usually.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.600
Wait a minute, I switched topics.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.200
It became about the
economy. These kids today!

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.530
This reminds me, and this
is just completely random,

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.810
but you know that Sona
used to play dodgeball.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.643
Yeah.

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:28.530
Back in the day, pre-podcast,

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.410
this is before you met your
husband, the wonderful Tak.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.243
Mm-hmm.

00:03:32.243 --> 00:03:34.260
Sona was in a dodgeball league.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.093
Yeah.

00:03:35.093 --> 00:03:35.926
And the thing I remember the most

00:03:35.926 --> 00:03:38.490
is every time I asked
her, "How did it go?"

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.830
She'd say, "Ugh, I got red carded."

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:41.663
Yeah.

00:03:41.663 --> 00:03:44.577
Because she was constantly
losing it on people.

00:03:44.577 --> 00:03:45.410
I was.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.040
And this is something
that I wanna explain,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.680
because people listen to the podcast,

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.427
and I've had people come up to me and say,

00:03:51.427 --> 00:03:53.010
"Oh, you know, Sona's such a saint

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.725
that she puts up with your foolishness."

00:03:54.725 --> 00:03:56.520
Oh, you wanna destroy that right now?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.900
No, no, not destroy it.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.987
But people have this idea that,

00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:01.800
"Oh, Sona's got a book out
that's doing really well."

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.970
New York Times bestseller.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.917
What they don't--
I'm an author.

00:04:04.917 --> 00:04:05.750
Mm. Really?

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.260
Is New York Times bestseller really a way

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.550
to tell how a book's doing?

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.590
Oh wait.
(Sona laughing)

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.270
It says here it's exactly the way

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.400
to tell how a book's doing.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.570
It's actually New York Times

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.090
with just a watch store in Times Square.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.590
It's on their bestseller list.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.160
No, but, she's had all this success

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.840
and she's got her own-- you're
probably selling foods now

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.337
on the Internet.
[Matt] Oh yeah.

00:04:29.337 --> 00:04:30.630
I'm doing the least amount of work I can.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.300
But anyway, people don't realize

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.115
that Sona has a terrible temper
and you can hear it snap.

00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:39.060
that Sona has a terrible temper
and you can hear it snap.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.020
Had.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.910
You had, now, did it go away?

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.110
It--
Be honest.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.540
There's very few people
that can bring it out of me,

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.520
and you are one of them.
Oh.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.870
For the most part, I'm pleasant

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.847
to everybody else, except--

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.590
Like, this?

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.483
I'm just putting a finger up.

00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:54.870
I know.
To make a point!

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:55.703
I know.

00:04:55.703 --> 00:04:58.980
But you do things and you just
press these little buttons.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.813
Okay.

00:04:59.813 --> 00:05:03.330
And you know what to do,
and I start to see red.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.730
But, be honest.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:09.390
Would you say that when
you would lose your temper,

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:12.600
this is before this wonderful
life that you have now,

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.900
you had really--
I'd go fucking crazy.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.160
[Conan] You'd go fucking crazy.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.633
And I've seen it happen.
I never got physical.

00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:22.080
I never got physical, I
never got into a fight.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.780
But I've yelled at a lot of people.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:25.613
Yeah.

00:05:25.613 --> 00:05:26.446
[Sona] And, you know, yeah, I have.

00:05:26.446 --> 00:05:29.850
But I think now, I've seen her transform.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.150
I haven't seen that side
of you in quite awhile.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.040
I do breathing exercises now.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.070
That's serious. I do breathing exercises.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.360
And this is for your temper?

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.593
Yeah.
Have your kids seen it?

00:05:40.593 --> 00:05:42.087
Have they seen mom lose it yet?

00:05:42.087 --> 00:05:45.303
No, no, I really don't wanna
lose it in front of them.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.030
If I'm on the road and I'm driving

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.730
and someone cuts me off or upsets me,

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:53.490
I just immediately just start breathing,

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.480
if someone pisses me off.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.670
I've been in the passenger seat with Sona

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.950
when someone would just
slightly cut us off

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:02.280
and what she always
says, which is the clue

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.680
that she's been triggered, is, "Really!?"

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.330
She goes, "Really!?"

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.210
And then suddenly you're Gene Hackman

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:11.040
in The French Connection.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.370
You're driving about 150 miles an hour

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.620
through 1970s New York,

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.760
which is strange.
Wow, impressive.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.490
Yeah, she actually changes
the time space around us,

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.320
and you're going under
that raised subway--

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.700
There's a guy in a Santa suit.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.750
And, yeah, exactly.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.520
And she's like--
(high-pitched grunt)

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.980
And then we're going and I'm with her.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.560
A national treasure.
(Sona scoffing)

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.154
Who could be lost at any moment.

00:06:33.154 --> 00:06:33.987
Oh, God.

00:06:33.987 --> 00:06:36.720
But anyway, it's horrifying.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:37.553
[Sona] Well, don't--

00:06:37.553 --> 00:06:38.400
But you're not that person anymore.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.940
I'm not, but can you admit
that you do things sometimes

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.170
to just rile me up?

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.790
My guest today is a very funny

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.560
actor/comedian.
Ohh...

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.633
We gotta get going, don't we?

00:06:47.633 --> 00:06:49.650
I know, but you know
you do. You know you do.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.330
Nope, not at all.
You know you do.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.650
Nope.
He's doing it right now.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:53.940
You're doing it right now.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.312
Maybe a little less gabby gabby right now?

00:06:56.312 --> 00:06:57.820
Oh, go, Sona, go!

00:06:57.820 --> 00:06:59.649
(Sona laughing)
Unleash! Go!

00:06:59.649 --> 00:07:00.720
It's like the Hulk.
[Matt] Let it out.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.033
Maybe!
Let it out!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.880
Maybe you should just--
(Sona laughing)

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.120
[Matt] I think the Cones
is laughing at you.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:07.953
[Conan] Maybe a little less talky walky?

00:07:07.953 --> 00:07:08.786
I can't. I'm gonna breathe.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.768
Maybe a little less... Sona talk.

00:07:14.768 --> 00:07:16.620
(Sona exhaling)
(Matt laughing)

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.150
That's a breathing exercise?

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.080
Yeah, I think you're giving birth.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.580
You're like a hobo sleeping
under an apple tree.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.180
(Conan exhaling)

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.361
That was a good pie I stole!

00:07:26.361 --> 00:07:29.520
(Sona laughing)
(Conan exhaling)

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.860
Oh, you're the worst, you
know that you are the worst.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:34.010
You know that you are,
that's okay, though.

